00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:55.840
On the other hand, the

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:01.840
Connect server, you need
to specify where it is.

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:05.430
So I'm going to just go to
the app, refresh a little bit.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:08.197
And you also have
to pay attention

00:15:08.197 --> 00:15:10.030
to the virtual environment
because in Python

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:10.750
it is very important.

00:15:10.750 --> 00:15:12.292
You want to isolate
your environment.

00:15:12.292 --> 00:15:16.720
So that you have sufficient
package isolation.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:19.290
And so what Connect does
at this point is that when

00:15:19.290 --> 00:15:23.820
you send the command and it
uses the rsconnect package,

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.340
right? This
rsconnect-python package allows

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:29.310
you to programmatically
deploy the content

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:31.240
to Connect using a command line.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:35.465
And it wraps your
content into a bundle

00:15:35.465 --> 00:15:36.840
first and uploads
the bundle that

00:15:36.840 --> 00:15:40.300
includes the application itself,
the requirements dot text.

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:43.650
So that Connect first will
look for the compatible Python

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:45.630
version on the
server itself and it

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:49.350
will use the compatible version
of Python to run the app

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:52.230
and uses the
requirements dot text

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:53.860
to rebuild the environment.

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:56.050
So each deployment is sandboxed.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.390
It is robust against
future deployments.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:00.400
It does not impact
previous deployments.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.990
It guarantees to
run all the time.

00:16:01.990 --> 00:16:03.910
So that is really handy for us.

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:05.940
And, and at the end,
